==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*skīnan}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*skīnaną}}, from an {{der|ang|ine-pro|*(s)ḱeh₁y-}}.

Cognate with {{cog|ofs|skīna}} ({{cog|fy|skine}}, {{m|fy|skyne}}), {{cog|osx|skīnan}} ({{cog|nds|schienen}}), {{cog|odt|skīnan}} ({{cog|nl|schijnen}}), {{cog|goh|skīnan}} ({{cog|de|scheinen}}), {{cog|non|skína}} ({{cog|da|skinne}}, {{cog|sv|skina}}), {{cog|got|𐍃𐌺𐌴𐌹𐌽𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|grc|σκιά}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*sěnь}} ({{cog|ru|сень}}).

